          "x": 18,
          "y": 92,
          "x_evidence": "ServiceTitan is not SMB-native. One analyst report describes it as beginning in the mid-market (4–40 technicians) before 'strategically moving upmarket to enterprise customers.' Its $10,000+ annualized billings threshold for an 'active customer' skews its count toward larger accounts. Its pricing ($250–$398+/month) and onboarding complexity make it poorly suited to solo and small operators without dedicated staff, per multiple 2025 review roundups. Scored on shipped surface.",
          "y_evidence": "ServiceTitan has the highest scalability ceiling in this set. Recent customers include 30+ branch and 50-location roofing expansion operators (TIMEPROOFUSA and Master Roofing Solutions, SPS PoolCare with 30+ branches, Azureon with 11 locations). The platform supports multiple trades, multi-location operations, enterprise reporting, and accounting integration. Its SEC FY2025 annual report describes it as expanding scalability as a core priority. Scored on shipped surface.",
